Subject: utility.c: no ~user expansion on wasi (no passwd database)

ExpandFilename() expands a leading "~user/" through getpwnam()/struct passwd.
wasi-libc has no <pwd.h> (patch 0001 stops studio.h from including it), so the
block does not compile.  WASI's capability model has no home directories at
all, so the correct behaviour is simply to leave "~user/..." untouched -- which
is what the function already does when the block is compiled out.

Plain "~/" (no user name) is handled by the other branch of the if and is
unaffected.

--- a/MagickCore/utility.c
+++ b/MagickCore/utility.c
@@ -657,7 +657,7 @@
     }
   else
     {
-#if defined(MAGICKCORE_POSIX_SUPPORT) && !defined(__OS2__)
+#if defined(MAGICKCORE_POSIX_SUPPORT) && !defined(__OS2__) && !defined(__wasi__)
       char
 #if defined(MAGICKCORE_HAVE_GETPWNAM_R)
         buffer[MagickPathExtent],
